invariant: INV-48
file: mlkem.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: mlkem.h's entries pick the copy for the four-way Keccak on
  CH_CPU_VAES, so a session that states AVX2 alone runs mlkem.c and
  one that states VAES runs the copy. The bytes are the same.
  bin/x86_kernels_test counts the copy's calls under every
  ch_cfg.cpu value, and test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh builds it for
  x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without
  docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX2) != 0;
--- new
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_VAES) != 0;
